{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509002461,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEzMTEzNTIxNTc="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509002462,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEzMTEzNTIxNTg="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1509003886,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzOTU4MDUxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-339580512"},"message":"Sounds like a nice-to-have to me, but I think this would need some kind of configurable behavior of `AutomagicIO`, determining what to patch and what to possibly exclude. I doubt every code people might want to use with datalad is easy with auto-getting things whenever `exists` is called for example.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1509004346,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzOTU4MjIzMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-339582232"},"message":"A little more on the point of `exists`:\nAs of now, code using `exists` could be executed in a way that it's doing stuff only, if the file is present in a V5 repo without adapting that code. Could be nice in some cases. With the enhancement you propose, that kind of code would need to be rewritten to use our `file_has_content`.\n\nI guess there are cases where it'S nice to have that enhancement and cases where it actually increases the effort. So, providing a config or parameters to adjust the behavior would allow for more code to seamlessly being used with datalad.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1509016130,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzOTYzMTc2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-339631765"},"message":"Side note: the last problem with AutomagicIO somewhat undermined my trust into the approach of it is used within the code eg as a context manager (not as python -m datalad for the entire process) - we might be too late to monkey patch of those functions already imported and bound locally (eg from io import open). \nThe only generic python level solution there would be to somehow change the actual code behind those functions but I am not sure if it is possible. More reliable way could be to overload those few syscalls which lie beneath all of them, but I don't know how feasible that would be to do at runtime, and smells like a generic fuse system for annex.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1517356898,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MTc3NjgxMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-361776810"},"message":"Any updates on this front? I too rely on code that often tries `exists` prior to `open`, so in some cases AutoMagic is not an option for me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1517370511,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MTgxNTIxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-361815212"},"message":"Would it be too much to ask to try 0.9.x branch version? We should release that one very soon, and knowing that it covers your usecase would be great. exist check should work https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/0.9.x/datalad/auto.py","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1517376079,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MTgyNzEwMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-361827101"},"message":"I'll give that a shot, thanks!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1517528902,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MjQ0MDAyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-362440025"},"message":"I tried 0.9.x branch, and using `isfile` was useful for getting file, and `exists` also worked. However, a related issue I'm having is that it seems not all packages deal well with symlinks. For example, the mime library (which `pliers` uses when opening files), return type 'inode/symlink' rather than the type of the file under version control. \n\nThus, I would normally `get` and `unlock` each file manually prior to calling pliers. Any tips here for avoiding that? It's not the end of the world but ideally I'd like my code to be datalad agnostic. Thanks!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1517538999,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MjQ2ODE0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-362468148"},"message":"thanks for the report @adelavega again.  Workaround is obvious -- dereference the link\n```ipython\nIn [11]: import magic  # requires libmagic, so import here\n    ...: print magic.from_file(os.path.realpath('sub-01_inplaneT2.nii.gz'), mime=True)\napplication/gzip\n```\nbut it should imho be done as an option to the `from_file` call similarly to `file` command in cmdline having `--dereference` (ref: https://github.com/ahupp/python-magic/issues/159), although it is quite cheap/easy to call realpath yourself.  One way (annex) or another (just a regular symlink) imho pliers should not care about discovering the symlinks but should care about content.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1517542324,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MjQ3NTk1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-362475952"},"message":"Yes I agree. I think I'll patch that function in pliers then! Thanks.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1517612346,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MjczMzYxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-362733616"},"message":"Actually this does not work. If the file is not downloaded yet, pointing to realpath will not trigger `get`, and thus will return a `FileNotFound` error. In contrast, giving the original symlink path *will* trigger `get` but since magic looks at the symlink, it returns mimetype symlink. \n\nFor now, I will explore changing pliers to use `isfile` instead of `exists` as a workaround. Thanks!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1517613205,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MjczNjYxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-362736611"},"message":"yes, those are 2 'orthogonal' issues\n- `isfile` to trigger download\n- `realpath` to magic.mime content instead of symlink","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540753137,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzczMTg2OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1924#issuecomment-433731868"},"message":"I think we have moved away from automagicio as a whole -- at least for now.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540753137,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTkzMDkxMzQxMg=="},"status":2}]}